# Testing Rules

## Structure
- AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert (blank lines between)
- One logical assertion per test (multiple #expect calls fine if testing one behavior)
- Descriptive names: "should reject expired tokens" not "test1"

## Swift Testing
- Use @Suite and @Test, not XCTest
- In-memory ModelContainer: `ModelConfiguration(isStoredInMemoryOnly: true)`
- @MainActor on all SwiftData tests
- Use Tiempo.Category (not Category) to avoid ObjC name collision

## Boundaries
- Mock at system boundaries (network, filesystem, time) — not internal modules
- For SwiftData: use real in-memory containers, not mocks
- Test both success and failure paths for async code

## What to Test
- Engine logic (TimeEntryEngine, ScheduleEngine, AccountabilityEngine, GoalsEngine)
- Model computed properties (duration, formattedDuration)
- Edge cases: empty inputs, nil values, boundary conditions
